nt shall cooperate with and\nL573@P19: provide assistance to Consultant in responding to any such investigation in such manner as\nL574@P19: Consultant elects in its sole and exclusive discretion.\nL575@P19: (b) The Parties acknowledge and agree that the added services shall require Consultant to register and\nL576@P19: comply with the Foreign Agents Registration Act (FARA) for those specific added services.\nL577@P19: Consultant will prepare and file all necessary filings and reports pursuant to FARA in connection\nL578@P19: with the added services, and Client will be responsible for and pay the initial FARA registration\nL579@P19: fee of $305, and $305 or such other amount as may be amended from time to time by law for each\nL580@P19: supplemental filing, if any, in addition to any other filing fees, costs, and expenses related to\nL581@P19: compliance in anyjurisdiction. Fees and expenses shall continue to be paid by Client per the terms\nL582@P19: of the Agreement, and as applicable and allocated to the added services, and all receipts,\nL583@P19: disbursements, and activities will be properly reported.\nL584@P19: This AMENDMENT NO. 1 TO CONSULTING SERVICES AGREEMENT (“Amendment”) is made and\nL585@P19: entered into as of April 15, 2025, to amend that certain Consulting Services Agreement dated February 1,\nL586@P19: 2025 (the “Agreement”), by and between Mercury Public Affairs LLC (“Consultant”) and PRVO\nL587@P19: PLINARSKO DRUSTVO d.o.o. (PPD Group) (“Client”), each ofwhich may be referred to as a “Party,”\nL588@P19: or together as the “Parties.”\nL589@P19: It is the intent ofthe Parties to confirm the Agreement and its terms, and modify and amend the Agreement\nL590@P19: related to the following terms only: add additional services, provide compliance terms for additional\nL591@P19-20: services.Received by NSD/FARA Registration Unit 05/06/2025 9:48:54 AM\nL592@P20: Jolw T. Lowwan\nL593@P20: John F. Lonergan (Apr 25, 202^18:12 E 18:12 EDT)\nL594@P20: By:\nL595